<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">11 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 11 July, from 1302 to 1979.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1302 <span class="tih-ago">724 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Flemish militia defeat French knights at the Battle of the Golden Spurs</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Flemish townsmen on foot routed the French cavalry at Courtrai, collecting hundreds of golden spurs from the dead. The battle showed that disciplined infantry could beat mounted knights.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/golden-bull-of-1356" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/golden-bull-of-1356.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1346 <span class="tih-ago">680 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles of Luxembourg is elected King of the Romans</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Five prince-electors meeting at Rhens chose Charles of Luxembourg as rival king to Louis IV. Later crowned emperor as Charles IV, he issued the Golden Bull of 1356 that fixed imperial elections for centuries.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-bull-of-1356">Golden Bull of 1356</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iv">Charles IV</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1798 <span class="tih-ago">228 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress re-establishes the US Marine Corps</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An Act of Congress created the US Marine Corps as a permanent service, reviving the Continental Marines of the Revolution. It grew into one of America's most celebrated fighting forces.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1804 <span class="tih-ago">222 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Aaron Burr mortally wounds Alexander Hamilton in a duel</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Vice President Aaron Burr shot Alexander Hamilton at Weehawken, New Jersey; Hamilton died the next day. The death of the first Treasury Secretary ended Burr's political career.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/boston" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boston.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1914 <span class="tih-ago">112 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Babe Ruth makes his major league debut for the Red Sox</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Nineteen-year-old Babe Ruth pitched for the Boston Red Sox against Cleveland, winning his first major league game. He went on to become baseball's greatest slugger and a symbol of the 1920s.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/australia" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/australia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1979 <span class="tih-ago">47 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Skylab falls to Earth over Western Australia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">NASA's Skylab space station broke up on re-entry, scattering debris near Esperance in Western Australia. The local shire jokingly fined NASA for littering; an American radio host paid the fine in 2009.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a></div></div></li></ol>
